{"availability":"available","full":"JakeChampion/lang","name":"lang","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-06T07:50:20Z","updated":"2026-10-17T15:46:37Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://jakechampion.github.io/lang/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:50.017Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:50.017Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:50.017Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:46.323Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.320Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:29.259Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:03:25.753Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:59.608Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T13:21:39.137Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T16:01:50.017Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fern is a small, statically typed, general-purpose language that compiles to a static native binary or to WebAssembly from the same source. It has no runtime to boot and no garbage collector: memory is reference counted, with the counting largely elided at compile time. A hello-world binary is a few kilobytes and startup is the kernel's exec followed by your main.","The compiler is a single binary. It parses, type-checks, optimises, assembles, and links in-process, so building a program needs nothing on PATH but fern itself. The same binary formats, lints, type-checks, interprets, resolves packages, and reports what capabilities a package reaches.","Documentation: (tutorial · reference · standard library · playground · why Fern)"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JakeChampion/lang/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"92e686c672dad147341654dd029ef86ccc8bef51d6515392b45cccfaed9b7ba8","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:50.157Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:50.157Z","projectInsights":{"version":